id: ops-to4t
title: Duplication gate scans generated PM extension copies
description: "The real pm-ops release gate reports thousands of clone pairs against .agents/pm/extensions/pm-ops after PM extension installation, despite the directory being ignored runtime state. This blocks an otherwise clean release and makes local and CI results depend on extension activation."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-26T16:52:31.639Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-26T17:13:46.466Z"
assignee: codex
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A real generated extension copy is excluded from the duplication scan; a fixture proves the tracked source remains in scope; npm run duplication reports 0 clone pairs and the full release gate passes.
repro_steps: "Install or activate pm-ops into .agents/pm/extensions/pm-ops, then run npm run duplication; jscpd reports source versus generated extension clone pairs."
expected_result: "The duplication gate scans tracked TypeScript source and tests, excludes generated PM extension cache, and still fails for real tracked clones."
actual_result: "Before the fix, 38.34% duplicated lines were reported from generated extension copies; after excluding that directory, the tracked source scan reports zero clones."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
