notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T16:55:01.199Z","harness:codex","The initial full release gate failed at 38.34% duplicated lines when the installed PM extension cache was scanned. After excluding only .agents/pm/extensions, the real jscpd gate reported 0% duplicated lines, 43 tracked TypeScript sources, and 0 clone pairs. The fixture proves tracked source is still analyzed."
  "2026-09-26T16:57:52.338Z","harness:codex","Final npm run release:check exit 0: 0% duplicated lines across 43 TypeScript sources; fixture verifies ignored generated extension cache and analyzed tracked source; measured all-source coverage 100/100/100/100. npm audit --omit=dev reports 0 vulnerabilities."
  "2026-09-26T17:13:46.442Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review on pm-ops PR 124 found that matchedSources.length alone did not prove jscpd analyzed lines. The real fixture now asserts report.totalLines > 0; the focused jscpd test and duplication gate pass. The post-review full npm run release:check exits 0 with measured 100/100/100/100 coverage. A new exact-head review is required after push."
